additional fee of EGP 25,000. * UAE: USPTO and UAE have signed a joint =
agreement to expedite patent granting process. The UAE will now accept =
positive patent examination results from the USPTO, which will =
significantly speed up the patent-granting process in the UAE. | A =
Cabinet Decision has been issued in March 2025 detailing the =
establishment and operational framework for the Industrial Property =
Grievances Committee. * Zanzibar: On 18 July 2025, the Zanzibar IP =
Office announced the implementation of increased official fees, set to =
take effect from 11 August 2025. These revised fees will apply =
retrospectively to both new and pending applications, where official =
fees remain outstanding on or after this date. * Bahrain: Bahrain and =
Japan Sign MoU to Launch PPH Program, set to launch on January 1, 2026. =
| Bahrain PTO launched PPH Pilot Programs with South Korea (effective =
January 15, 2025, for three years) and the European Patent Office =
(commenced March 1, 2025, for an initial two years). | Bahrain Patent =
Office recently signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with the =
USPTO to implement the Patent Prosecution Highway (PPH) system. Bahrain =
has signed a Patent Prosecution Highway (PPH) Agreement with China. PPH =
pilot program officially started on May 1, 2024, and will run for five =
years until April 30, 2029. * Myanmar: Myanmar=E2=80=99s Patent Law 2019 =
came into effect on 31 May 2024. However, it is important to note that =
patent applications cannot yet be filed, as the issuance of patent forms =
and fees remains pending. * Qatar: MOCI announced that it has started =
accepting applications for industrial designs and models as of 26 =
October 2025. | Qatar PTO has issued a significant clarification =
regarding the payment of annuity fees. The Office has resumed accepting =
annuity payments on all patent applications, irrespective of their =
acceptance or grant status. This change overrules the previous policy =
that deferred fees beyond the third year for pending applications. * =
ARIPO: China National Intellectual Property Administration (CNIPA) has =
recently introduced the China-Africa Patent Prosecution Highway (PPH) in =
collaboration with the African Regional Intellectual Property =
Organization (ARIPO). * Algeria: Algeria has introduced 19% VAT on =
Official Fees associated with Intellectual Property Services. * Saudi =
Arabia: Saudi Arabia recently joined the Hague Agreement for =
International Design Registration | In accordance with the amended =
Patent and Industrial Design Law, validity of industrial designs has =
been extended from ten (10) to fifteen (15) years for all designs =
submitted in 2013 and onwards. | Saudi Authority for Intellectual =
Property (SAIP) has signed a Patent Prosecution Highway (PPH) Agreement =
with Intellectual Property Office of Singapore (IPOS). This PPH Pilot =
Program commenced on 12 September 2023 for a period of 2 years and will =
end on 11 September 2025. From: =D0=9C=D0=B8=D1=85=D0=B0=D0=B8=D0=BB =
